cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the archived release using
  the metadata in this file.
title: >-
  Analysis code for null-hypothesis tests of an anomalous pixel
  group in a single photograph
abstract: >-
  R code implementing three component null-hypothesis tests of
  whether an anomalous group of bright pixels in a single
  photograph is consistent with sensor noise, lens-flare
  ghosting, or ordinary scene lighting in a shaded tree line.
  Includes veiling-glare correction, a generalized Pareto scan
  statistic with look-elsewhere correction, and a sensitivity
  analysis across detection thresholds and tail quantiles. The
  source photograph is distributed with the code so that the
  analysis is reproducible as published.
type: software
